messages:
Eli (design): Dropped a small theme pass to staging — main goals: improve inline token contrast, tame codeblock glow, and pick a chart palette that's CVD-friendly. Added before/after screenshots and a short CSS diff. Hoping for quick eyeballs across OSes.

Priya: On it. In staging the code token still reads faint on smaller widths, especially when the panel has the semi-transparent layer. Also the panel alpha makes the header labels jitter when scrolled.

Samir: Chart feedback: the stacked area gradients look muddy when multiple series overlap. For small multiples we should use flat fills + different strokes. Also consider a neutral baseline color for zero lines.

Jo: UX nit: focus ring on dropdowns is currently thin and navy, which disappears on darker gradients. Can we use a thicker high-contrast ring for keyboard nav? Also copy: "Show token usage" -> "Show token usage details" in the usage panel.

Luca: Quick palette suggestion: move token highlight from #FFD95B to #CE9E00 or #C79100. Need to check for vibrancy on OLED.

theme-bot: contrast-result: #FFD95B on #0E1116 => 2.6:1; #CE9E00 => 4.2:1; #C79100 => 4.5:1. note: OLED boost may increase perceived saturation.

Priya: Prefer #C79100 for accessibility, but let's desaturate a touch on mobile to avoid color bleed. Also, reduce the code-block outer blur to 6px -> 3px and lower opacity to 0.35.

Eli (design): Agreed on #C79100. For charts I'm proposing this set: teal, steel blue, violet, amber, coral — spaced by hue and checked for deutan/protan. Will add shape markers for small series.

Eli (design): CSS snippet in the PR: ```
:root{
  --bg:#0E1116;
  --panel:rgba(16,18,22,0.78);
  --code-bg:#0b0f12;
  --code-glow:rgba(199,153,0,0.12);
  --token:#C79100;
  --chart-1:#36D6D0;
  --chart-2:#4B7CE6;
  --chart-3:#9B7CFB;
  --chart-4:#F0B23A;
  --chart-5:#FB7A8E;
  --focus-ring: 0 0 0 3px rgba(42,111,255,0.22);
}
```

theme-bot: cvd-simulation: primary palette readable on deutan/protan; chart-4 vs chart-5 reduced delta on low-saturation displays but shape markers help.

Samir: For tiny line charts, use solid 2px strokes and toggle anti-aliasing off for pixel-perfect rendering at small heights. Also bump point radius from 3px -> 4px on touch devices.

Jo: Thanks. I'll update the copy suggestions and add alt text for all decorative thumbnails in the modal. Also add "High Contrast" toggle in accessibility settings to switch to a 7:1 scheme.

Luca: Can someone test on Linux with fractional scaling? I've seen token hue shift slightly with gamma differences.

Eli (design): Plan: swap token -> #C79100, apply reduced code glow, adopt flat fills for small multiple charts with shape markers, and bump focus ring to 3px semi-opaque blue. I'll open the PR and attach screenshots for: mac retina, win125%, ubuntu fractional. Tagging QE.

Priya: LGTM. I'll push the copy edits inline in the PR and run a quick axe run on staging.

Eli (design): Great — thanks everyone. If you spot any flicker or readability regressions in the next hour drop screenshots here and I'll iterate.
